t's in description.\n\nKeep it focused.\n\nunit_id: leave null everywhere (not certain of unitsdb IDs). For m³, could be \"u:metre_cubed\"? Not certain — leave null per rule.\n\nStructure check for type_level entries: {\"maximum_capacity\": {\"value\": ..., \"unit_symbol\": ..., \"unit_id\": null, \"footnote_markers\": []}}. Rule 2 shape includes footnote_markers; include empty array or omit when none? \"footnote_markers\": [\"1)\"] shown; for none, I can omit or []. I'll omit footnote_markers when empty to reduce noise? The shape says MUST be object with that shape, separating value from unit. I'll include footnote_markers only when present, and include unit_id: null. Hmm — to be safe, include all four keys? That's verbose. The R60 example in rules shows {\"model\": \"Emax=25t\", \"value\": 25} without unit objects. For type_level I'll include value, unit_symbol, unit_id (null), and footnote_markers only if present. I'll include footnote_markers: [] omitted. Let me just include value, unit_symbol, unit_id for all; add footnote_markers where applicable (none here).\n\nCertificate page_total: 12 — from footer \"Page 1 of 12 pages\".\n\noiml_issuer_id: not given; omit.\n\nNow output JSON.\n\nmodels list: {\"model_id\": \"DN15\"}, etc. Should model_id be like \"DN15\" or \"Qalcosonic W1 DN15\"? model_id \"DN15\" is fine; family_name \"Qalcosonic W1\".\n\nbattery_configuration values — note the typo in source: first bullet \"AA:size\" garbled. I'll normalize to two AA.\n\nOne consideration: the second bullet duplicates DN15/20/25/32 with + one \"A23\" — possibly intended \"for DN40...\" variants, but the source clearly repeats. I'll represent as options.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-A-SK1-2023.02 Rev. 1\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"TK-P05-85\",\n    \"page_total\": 12,\n    \"member_state\": \"Slovakia\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2023-05-25\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Slovak Legal 